<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">20 August in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">9 events that happened on 20 August, from 636 to 1998.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">636 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,390 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Arab armies defeat the Byzantines at the Yarmouk</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After six days of fighting, the Muslim Arab army under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalid-ibn-al-walid">Khalid ibn al-Walid</a> destroyed the Byzantine forces near the River Yarmouk. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/byzantine-empire">Byzantium</a> lost <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a> for good.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khalid-ibn-al-walid">Khalid ibn al-Walid</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/palestine">Palestine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/917">917 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,109 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Simeon I's Bulgarians rout the Byzantine army at Achelous</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the Achelous river near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/black-sea">Black Sea</a> coast, Bulgarian forces under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tsar">Tsar</a> Simeon I won a decisive victory over the Byzantine army, one of its worst disasters. The battle made Simeon de facto ruler of almost the whole Balkan Peninsula.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/simeon-i-of-bulgaria">Simeon I of Bulgaria</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thrace">Thrace</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1119">1119 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">907 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Henry I of England defeats Louis VI of France at Brémule</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vexin">Norman Vexin</a>, Henry I of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a>, duke of Normandy, defeated <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-vi-of-france">Louis VI of France</a>, who backed the claim of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-clito">William Clito</a>. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prince-henry-the-navigator">Henry</a>'s largely dismounted knights routed the French cavalry, Louis barely escaped, and Henry's hold on Normandy was secured.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-bremule">Battle of Brémule</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/louis-vi-of-france">Louis VI of France</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1191">1191 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">835 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Richard I has 2,700 Muslim prisoners executed at Ayyadieh</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">When negotiations with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a> over ransom and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/true-cross">True Cross</a> stalled, Richard the Lionheart had the captured garrison of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/acre">Acre</a> killed outside the city. The massacre embittered the war.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/kingdom-of-england">Kingdom of England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/true-cross">True Cross</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1308">1308 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">718 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Papal investigators record the Templar leaders' absolution in the Chinon Parchment</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Three papal investigators, among them Cardinal Bérenger Frédol, ended their interrogation of the Templar leaders and wrote the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chinon">Chinon</a> Parchment, recording that the accused had confessed, done penance and been absolved of heresy. The order was disbanded in 1312.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/knights-templar">Knights Templar</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1882">1882 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">144 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Tchaikovsky's 1812 Overture has its premiere in Moscow</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyotr-ilyich-tchaikovsky">Tchaikovsky</a>'s overture marking <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russia">Russia</a>'s defeat of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a> was first performed in a tent near the unfinished Cathedral of Christ the Saviour. Its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/field-artillery">cannon</a> and bells made it a perennial favourite.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1940">1940 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">86 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Leon Trotsky is struck with an ice axe in Mexico City</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Soviet agent Ramón Mercader attacked <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/leon-trotsky">Leon Trotsky</a> in his study in Coyoacán; Trotsky died the next day. Stalin had pursued his exiled rival for over a decade.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mexico-city">Mexico City</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1968">1968 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">58 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Warsaw Pact armies invade Czechoslovakia</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hundreds of thousands of Soviet-led troops crossed into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a> overnight to end <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-dubcek">Alexander Dubček</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/prague-spring">Prague Spring</a> reforms. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> soon claimed the right to intervene in any socialist state.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/czechoslovakia">Czechoslovakia</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1998">1998 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">28 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US strikes al-Qaeda targets in Afghanistan and Sudan</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">In retaliation for the embassy bombings in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a>, US cruise missiles hit camps in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a> and the al-Shifa pharmaceutical factory in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khartoum">Khartoum</a>, whose link to weapons was disputed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a></div></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 20 August <span class="n">5</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/jacopo-peri"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/jacopo-peri.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Jacopo Peri</span><span class="tp">1561–1633</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bernardo-ohiggins"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bernardo-ohiggins.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bernardo O'Higgins</span><span class="tp">1778–1842</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/ton-duc-thang"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/ton-duc-thang.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Tôn Đức Thắng</span><span class="tp">1888–1980</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/slobodan-milosevic"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/slobodan-milosevic.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Slobodan Milošević</span><span class="tp">1941–2006</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rajiv-gandhi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rajiv-gandhi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Rajiv Gandhi</span><span class="tp">1944–1991</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 20 August <span class="n">8</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/eadberht-of-northumbria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/eadberht-of-northumbria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Eadberht of Northumbria</span><span class="tp">d. 768</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/bernard-of-clairvaux"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/bernard-of-clairvaux.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Bernard of Clairvaux</span><span class="tp">1090–1153</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/rognvald-kali-kolsson"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/rognvald-kali-kolsson.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Rögnvald Kali Kolsson</span><span class="tp">c. 1100–1158</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/borso-deste"><span class="ph ph-person" aria-hidden="true"></span><span><span class="nm">Borso d'Este</span><span class="tp">1413–1471</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/miguel-lopez-de-legazpi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/miguel-lopez-de-legazpi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Miguel López de Legazpi</span><span class="tp">c. 1502–1572</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/johan-de-witt"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/johan-de-witt.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Johan de Witt</span><span class="tp">1625–1672</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-pius-vii"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-pius-vii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Pius VII</span><span class="tp">1742–1823</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/meles-zenawi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/meles-zenawi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Meles Zenawi</span><span class="tp">1955–2012</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
